# =========================
# Dependencies
# =========================
node_modules/
# Ignored because these folders are extremely heavy and contain all downloaded packages. 
# They can be easily reproduced by running 'npm install' using the package.json and package-lock.json.

# =========================
# Environment Variables
# =========================
.env
.env.*.local
# Ignored because they contain highly sensitive data (database passwords, JWT secrets). 
# Committing these files is a major security risk. Only .env.example should be tracked.

# =========================
# Build Outputs
# =========================
frontend/dist/
backend/dist/
# Ignored because these are auto-generated files created during the build process (e.g., Vite build). 
# We only want to version the source code, not the compiled result.

# =========================
# AI Tools & IDE Configurations
# =========================
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
# Ignored to keep the repository clean. These are personal local settings for editors 
# and AI assistants that shouldn't be forced on other potential contributors.

# =========================
# Logs & OS Files
# =========================
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
# Ignored because these are system-specific junk files (macOS/Windows) or error logs 
# that provide no value to the project's source code.